commit 6a23daddf57075c6a65caa687420364ed42f2a67

C03: a first-person preference statement is a social turn, not a request (MEMORY1501)

MEMORY1245 measured that «Me gusta tomar café.» was taken as an order and the product asked where to go. `_personal_checkin_statement` now also reads a first-person taste or preference with nothing asked («me gusta/encanta…», «prefiero…», «I like/love/prefer…», without a «que» clause or a request head after it) as a social statement: conversation of the social kind with zero operations, the same route as «my day is going well».

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


